Article 1 (Purpose) The purpose of this Decree is to prescribe matters delegated by the Act on Local Government Subsidy Management and matters necessary for its enforcement.

Article 2 (Application to Education, Science, and Sports) In this Decree, with respect to matters concerning education, science, and sports or the special account for educational expenses, "head of a local government" shall be construed as "superintendent of education," "Minister of the Interior and Safety" as "Minister of Education," and "Ordinance of the Ministry of the Interior and Safety" as "Ordinance of the Ministry of Education."

Article 3 (Categories of Operating Expenses) Where subsidies are granted as operating expenses on a statutory basis under the former part of Article 6(2) of the Act on Local Government Subsidy Management (hereinafter "Act"), the categories of expenses that may be used as operating expenses are as follows. However, expenses under each subparagraph directly incurred in performing a local government subsidized project are excluded:
1. Personnel expenses;
2. Office management expenses;
3. Rental expenses;
4. Other expenses that the head of a local government considers particularly necessary for the basic operation of affairs or projects undertaken by another local government, corporation, organization, individual, or other person.

Article 4 (Management of Subsidy Histories)
① Under Article 6(3) of the Act, the head of a local government shall manage subsidy assistance histories separately for each project.
② Assistance histories under paragraph 1 shall include:
1. Project name;
2. The operator's name, trade name, and address; where the operator is a corporation or organization, its name and address;
3. Details of subsidies received by the operator during the preceding five years;
4. Results of performance evaluations under Article 27(1) of the Act.
③ Matters necessary for managing assistance histories other than those in paragraphs 1 and 2 shall be prescribed by Ordinance of the Ministry of the Interior and Safety.

Article 4-2 (Notification of Subsidy Budgets) When notifying the head of another local government of the preparation or adoption details of a subsidy budget bill under Article 6-2(1) and (2) of the Act, the head shall provide details separately for each project. The total subsidy amount shall also be notified.

Article 5 (Applications for Subsidy Grants) An application under Article 7(1) of the Act shall include:
1. The applicant's name, trade name, and address; where the operator is a corporation or organization, its name and address;
2. The project's purpose and details;
3. Project expenses and the amount of subsidy sought;
4. The amount to be borne by the applicant;
5. The scheduled dates of commencement and completion;
6. Other matters specified by the head as necessary for granting the subsidy.

Article 5-2 (Deposit and Grant of Subsidies)
① Subsidies that may be deposited in a local government's treasury for grant under Article 10-2(1) of the Act shall be subsidies other than:
1. Subsidies granted by the head of a local government to the head of another local government acting as an operator;
2. Subsidies granted to perform nationally subsidized projects.
② When depositing subsidies in the treasury under Article 10-2(1) of the Act, the head shall deposit them in a dedicated account opened in the name of the local government and used for subsidy grants.
③ An operator requesting grant of subsidies deposited in the treasury under Article 10-2(1) of the Act shall submit any of the following through the integrated local government subsidy management network under Article 28(1) of the Act (hereinafter "integrated local government subsidy management network") to the head:
1. Electronic invoices under the latter part of Article 163(1) of the Income Tax Act;
2. Electronic tax invoices under Article 32(2) of the Value-Added Tax Act;
3. Transaction approval statements for credit or debit cards issued for the purpose of using subsidies;
4. Other materials proving execution of subsidies.

Article 6 (Revocation of Grant Decisions Due to Changed Circumstances)
① "Cases prescribed by Presidential Decree" in Article 11(2) of the Act means either of the following:
1. Land, principal facilities, or other items necessary for project performance become unavailable for use or utilization for reasons not attributable to the operator;
2. Expenses other than the portion covered by subsidies, excluding expenses borne by the operator, cannot be procured for reasons not attributable to the operator.
② Subsidies to be granted under Article 11(4) of the Act shall cover:
1. Expenses necessary to remove machinery, equipment, or temporary buildings related to the project and to handle other remaining work;
2. Compensation payable upon cancellation of contracts concluded for project performance.

Article 7 (Retention of Project Materials) Materials to be retained by an operator under Article 16(3) of the Act are:
1. Accounts: documents aggregating by period the execution results of accounting affairs handled by the operator;
2. Evidentiary documents: documents proving the contents of the accounts under subparagraph 1;
3. Accompanying documents: documents necessary to explain the contents of accounts under subparagraph 1 or evidentiary documents under subparagraph 2.

Article 8 (Temporary Suspension of Project Performance)
① When temporarily suspending project performance under Article 16(5) of the Act, the head shall specify a period and require the operator to take measures complying with the details of the grant decision or an order under paragraph 4 of that Article.
② When requiring measures under paragraph 1, the head shall inform the operator that failure to take them may result in revocation of all or part of the grant decision under Article 12(1) of the Act.

Article 9 (Submission of Project Performance Reports)
① "Deadline prescribed by Presidential Decree" in the former part of the portion other than the subparagraphs of Article 17(1) of the Act means within two months after the date a ground in any subparagraph of that paragraph arises.
② "Where there is a ground prescribed by Presidential Decree" in the proviso to the portion other than the subparagraphs of Article 17(1) of the Act means where an operator, as a subsidized or indirectly subsidized operator under Article 2, subparagraph 3 or 6, of the Subsidy Management Act, has reported performance to the head through the integrated subsidy management network under Article 26-2(1) of that Act. <Amended October 4, 2023>
③ When preparing a project performance report under the former part of the portion other than the subparagraphs of Article 17(1) of the Act (hereinafter "performance report"), an operator shall clearly distinguish the details of use under the grant decision from the amount to be returned.
④ When reducing subsidies under Article 17(3) of the Act, the head shall apply the following ranges to the amount first granted after submission of the performance report: <Added October 4, 2023>
1. A submission delay of at least three months but less than six months: up to ten percent;
2. A delay of at least six months but less than 12 months: more than ten percent and up to 20 percent;
3. A delay of at least 12 months: more than 20 percent and up to 50 percent.

Article 10 (Verification of Settlement Reports)
① An auditor under Articles 2, subparagraph 7, and 9 of the Act on External Audit of Stock Companies, Etc. (hereinafter "auditor") verifying the appropriateness of a settlement report under the main clause of Article 17(2) of the Act (hereinafter "settlement report") shall prepare a related report. <Amended October 4, 2023>
② Necessary matters concerning the format, preparation method, items, and submission procedures of settlement reports and verification-related reports under paragraph 1 shall be prescribed by Ordinance of the Ministry of the Interior and Safety. <Amended October 4, 2023>

Article 11 (Selection of Auditors by Specified Operators)
① A specified local government subsidized operator under the main clause of Article 18(1) of the Act (hereinafter "specified operator") shall select an auditor within three months after receiving notice of the subsidy grant decision.
② An auditor selected under paragraph 1 shall conduct accounting audits in accordance with the auditing standards under Article 16 of the Act on External Audit of Stock Companies, Etc.
③ An audit report under the main clause of Article 18(1) of the Act (hereinafter "audit report") shall be prepared in accordance with Article 18 of the Act on External Audit of Stock Companies, Etc. However, necessary matters concerning detailed preparation methods, including forms of documents on matters to accompany the audit report, shall be prescribed by Ordinance of the Ministry of the Interior and Safety.
④ A specified operator shall submit the audit report to the head granting the subsidies within four months after the end of the relevant fiscal year.
⑤ Matters necessary for auditor selection procedures other than those in paragraph 1 shall be prescribed by Ordinance of the Ministry of the Interior and Safety.

Article 11-2 (Disclosure of Information by Operators)
① "Project of at least the scale prescribed by Presidential Decree" in the main clause of the portion other than the subparagraphs of Article 20-2(1) of the Act means a project for which total subsidies received from the head during the same fiscal year amount to at least five million won. However, where the project's characteristics require a different disclosure threshold, it means a project of at least the amount determined and publicly notified by the Minister of the Interior and Safety.
② "Deadline prescribed by Presidential Decree" in the main clause of the portion other than the subparagraphs of Article 20-2(1) of the Act means within four months after the end of the relevant fiscal year.
③ "Documents prescribed by Presidential Decree" in Article 20-2(1)5 of the Act means:
1. Where the main clause of Article 17(2) of the Act applies, documents on the results of verifying the appropriateness of the settlement report;
2. The operator's financial statements or final accounts;
3. Other documents determined and publicly notified by the Minister to enhance transparency of projects.
④ A corrective order issued to an operator under Article 20-2(2) of the Act shall be in writing, specifying its details, period, and other relevant matters.
⑤ When reducing subsidies under Article 20-2(2) of the Act, the head shall apply the following ranges to the total subsidies scheduled to be granted in the fiscal year disclosed under the main clause of paragraph 1 of that Article:
1. Failure to comply once with a corrective order under paragraph 4: up to ten percent;
2. Failure to comply twice: more than ten percent and up to 20 percent;
3. Failure to comply three or more times: more than 20 percent and up to 50 percent.

Article 12 (Property Subject to Disposal Restrictions)
① "Important property prescribed by Presidential Decree" in Article 21(1) of the Act means the following property (hereinafter "important property"):
1. Real estate and its accessories;
2. Vessels, buoys, floating piers, meaning structures floated on water to moor vessels or allow access to a quay, and floating docks, meaning floating facilities for building or repairing vessels or loading and unloading cargo, and their accessories;
3. Aircraft;
4. Other property that the head considers particularly necessary to achieve the purpose of the subsidy grant and publicly notifies.
② Under Article 21(1) of the Act, an operator shall record and maintain in books the current value and increases and decreases of important property by the method specified by the head, and report its status to the head every half year with documents necessary for its management.
③ The head shall disclose the status of important property through the local government's website or other means.
④ When ordering an operator to return all or part of the amounts in the subparagraphs of Article 21(5) of the Act under the portion other than those subparagraphs, the head shall provide written notice of the amount, calculation details, payment deadline, and other relevant matters. <Amended October 4, 2023>
⑤ When calculating amounts under Article 21(5)2 and 3 of the Act, if the head determines that the current value reported by the operator under paragraph 2 is significantly lower than present value considering market conditions and other factors, the head shall have an appraisal corporation under Article 29 of the Act on Appraisal and Certified Appraisers assess the present value of the property. <Amended October 4, 2023>

Article 13 (Cases Exempt from Disposal Restrictions) "Where grounds prescribed by Presidential Decree arise" in Article 21(4)3 of the Act means where a local government acting as operator acquires property for an amount less than 50 percent of the subsidy granted by another local government. <Amended October 4, 2023>

Article 14 Deleted. <October 4, 2023>

Article 15 (Exemptions from Committee Deliberation) "Cases prescribed by Presidential Decree" in the proviso to the portion other than the subparagraphs of Article 26(2) of the Act means any of the following: <Amended December 16, 2021>
1. Preparing a subsidy budget in accordance with the sharing of funding for a nationally subsidized project or a project subsidized by a Special Metropolitan City, Metropolitan City, Special Self-Governing City, Do, or Special Self-Governing Province (hereinafter "City/Do") under Article 23(2) of the Local Finance Act;
2. Submitting a revised budget bill to the local council under Article 142(4) of the Local Autonomy Act;
3. Preparing a supplementary revised budget bill under Article 145(1) of the Local Autonomy Act by reducing the unspent balance of the relevant year's subsidy budget.

Article 16 (Performance Evaluation and Management of Projects) The head of a local government shall register and manage results of performance evaluations under Article 27(1) of the Act (hereinafter "performance evaluations") in the integrated local government subsidy management network. <Amended May 16, 2023>

Article 16-2 (Establishment and Operation of the Integrated Local Government Subsidy Management Network)
① Where considered necessary for systematic and efficient operation under Article 28(1) of the Act, the Minister of the Interior and Safety may establish and implement detailed operating standards for the network.
② "Matters prescribed by Presidential Decree" in Article 28(2)8 of the Act means:
1. Revocation of subsidy grant decisions under Article 12 of the Act;
2. Publication of lists of persons improperly receiving subsidies under Article 30 of the Act;
3. Exclusion from project performance and restrictions on subsidy grants under Article 32 of the Act;
4. Recovery of subsidies under Article 34 of the Act;
5. Imposition and collection of sanction surcharges and additional charges under Article 35 of the Act;
6. Checking duplicate or improper receipt of subsidies;
7. Information by project unit for performing the following duties:
(a) Grant, execution, and settlement of subsidies;
(b) Verification of similarity or duplication of projects;
(c) Provision of tailored services to the public concerning projects.

Article 16-3 (Requests for Materials or Information)
① "Information prescribed by Presidential Decree" in Article 28-2(1)4(a) of the Act means:
1. Statements of real estate rental supply value under Article 55(2) of the Value-Added Tax Act;
2. Statements of financial position, comprehensive income, appropriation of retained earnings, or disposition of deficits under Article 60(2)1 of the Corporate Tax Act;
3. Statements of changes in stocks, etc., under Article 119(1) of the Corporate Tax Act;
4. Global income amounts under Article 14(2) of the Income Tax Act;
5. Gross revenue amounts under Article 24(1) of the Income Tax Act;
6. Materials submitted in payment statements under Article 164(1) of the Income Tax Act.
② "Materials or information prescribed by Presidential Decree" in Article 28-2(1)4(f) of the Act means:
1. Acquisition tax assessment materials under Article 7 of the Local Tax Act;
2. Property tax assessment materials under Article 105 of the Local Tax Act;
3. Motor vehicle tax assessment materials under Article 125 of the Local Tax Act.
③ "Materials or information prescribed by Presidential Decree" in Article 28-2(1)6 of the Act means the materials or information in attached Table 1.
④ Where considered necessary for efficient provision of materials or information requested under Article 28-2(1) of the Act, the Minister may promote linkage between the network and information systems related to such materials or information, in consultation with heads of relevant institutions.

Article 16-4 (Requests for Financial or Credit Information)
① When requesting financial information under Article 28-3(1)1 of the Act (hereinafter "financial information") or credit information under subparagraph 2 of that paragraph (hereinafter "credit information") from heads of financial institutions, etc., under that paragraph, the Minister and heads of local governments shall make the request in a document containing the following. "Financial institutions, etc." means financial companies, etc., under the Act on Real Name Financial Transactions and Confidentiality and credit information concentration institutions under Article 25 of the Credit Information Use and Protection Act; the same applies throughout this Article:
1. Name and resident registration number of the person in whose name the information is held; for a corporation, its name, representative's name, and corporate registration number;
2. Scope of the information, reference date for inquiry, and inquiry period.
② When providing financial or credit information under Article 28-3(3) of the Act, the head of a financial institution, etc., shall provide information including:
1. Name and resident registration number of the person in whose name it is held; for a corporation, its name, representative's name, and corporate registration number;
2. Name of the financial institution, etc., providing it;
3. Name of the relevant financial product and account number;
4. Contents of the financial or credit information.
③ Where considered necessary for efficient provision, the Minister and heads of local governments may request heads of financial institutions, etc., to provide information through the information and communications networks of associations, federations, central associations, or similar bodies to which they belong.

Article 16-5 (Exceptions to Destruction of Subsidy Management Information)
① "Materials or information prescribed by Presidential Decree" in the proviso to Article 28-5(1) of the Act means materials or information concerning:
1. Disposal of important property under Article 21 of the Act;
2. Matters under Article 16-2(2)1 through 6.
② When continuing to hold materials or information under the proviso to Article 28-5(2) of the Act, the Minister and heads of local governments shall store and manage them separately from other materials or information.

Article 17 (Methods for Publishing Lists)
① "Matters prescribed by Presidential Decree" in the portion other than the subparagraphs of Article 30(1) of the Act means:
1. Name, trade name, age, and address of the operator or subsidy recipient subject to publication (hereinafter "operators, etc."); for a corporation or organization, its name and address and its representative's name, age, and address;
2. Details of violations by the operators, etc., subject to publication;
3. Details of subsidy returns and sanction surcharges resulting from their violations;
4. Other matters the Local Government Subsidy Management Committee under Article 26 of the Act (hereinafter "Committee") considers necessary to make publication effective.
② The publication period under Article 30(1) of the Act shall be one year. If the head considers the violation serious, the period may be extended by up to one year following Committee deliberation.
③ "Where there are grounds prescribed by Presidential Decree, such as the death of the person making publication ineffective or publication being inappropriate" in Article 30(2) of the Act means:
1. The person subject to publication has died;
2. The person has been declared missing under Article 27 of the Civil Act;
3. Other cases in which the head, following Committee deliberation, considers publication to have no practical benefit.
④ To provide an opportunity to explain under Article 30(3) of the Act, the head shall notify the person in writing of the matters in the subparagraphs of paragraph 1 before convening the Committee.

Article 18 (Return of Subsidies) "Interest generated because of unavoidable grounds prescribed by Presidential Decree" in the proviso to Article 31(2) of the Act means:
1. Interest generated by subsidy amounts executed within one month after receipt;
2. Interest generated during delays in projects caused by natural disasters or other comparable grounds;
3. Interest generated during a period of improvement where statutory amendments or other reasons require improvement of execution methods after receipt of subsidies;
4. Interest generated for other reasons the head considers unavoidable in view of the project's characteristics.

Article 19 (Methods and Procedures for Exclusion from Project Performance)
① The period for excluding an operator from projects under the head's jurisdiction or restricting grants under Article 32(1) of the Act shall be as follows. However, where a violation under subparagraph 2 or 3 is considered to result from minor negligence or error, the period may be reduced by up to one half: <Added October 4, 2023>
1. A case under Article 32(1)1 of the Act: five years;
2. A case under Article 32(1)2 of the Act: three years;
3. A case under Article 32(1)3 of the Act: two years.
② "Welfare projects, nationally subsidized projects, or other projects prescribed by Presidential Decree" in Article 32(2) of the Act means: <Added October 4, 2023>
1. Welfare projects;
2. Nationally subsidized projects;
3. Other public-interest projects contributing to residents' convenience or regional development and prescribed by the local government's rules.
③ The period for restricting payments to a recipient under Article 32(3) of the Act shall be as follows. However, where a violation under subparagraph 2 or 3 is considered to result from minor negligence or error, the period may be reduced by up to one half: <Added October 4, 2023>
1. A case under Article 32(3)1 of the Act: five years;
2. A case under Article 32(3)2 of the Act: three years;
3. A case under Article 32(3)3 of the Act: one year.
④ The period for excluding an improper contracting enterprise under Article 32(5) of the Act (hereinafter "improper contracting enterprise") from project performance shall be: <Added October 4, 2023>
1. Where sentenced to imprisonment with or without labor for more than one year: five years;
2. Where sentenced to imprisonment with or without labor for one year or less: three years;
3. Where sentenced to a fine, limited to a fine not imposed together with imprisonment with or without labor: two years.
⑤ When excluding operators, etc., or improper contracting enterprises from project performance or restricting their grant or receipt of subsidies under Article 32(1) through (7) of the Act, the head shall immediately register the following in the integrated local government subsidy management network: <Amended October 4, 2023>
1. Name, trade name, resident registration number, business registration number, address, and license or registration numbers under relevant statutes of the operators, etc.; for a corporation, its name and corporate registration number and its representative's name and resident registration number;
2. Specific grounds for exclusion from performance or restrictions on grant or receipt;
3. Other matters prescribed by Ordinance of the Ministry of the Interior and Safety to facilitate execution of exclusion or restriction duties.
⑥ To prevent excluded or restricted operators, etc., or improper contracting enterprises from participating by changing trade names or representatives or similar means, the head shall, when deciding whether to grant or pay subsidies, check their resident registration numbers, corporate registration numbers, license or registration numbers under relevant statutes, and other relevant identifiers. <Amended October 4, 2023>
⑦ Detailed matters concerning notification contents and procedures for exclusion and restrictions, other than those in paragraphs 1 through 6, shall be prescribed by Ordinance of the Ministry of the Interior and Safety. <Amended October 4, 2023>

Article 20 (Notification of Orders to Return Subsidies) An operator ordering a recipient to return subsidies under Article 34(1) of the Act shall notify the head responsible for the project in writing, within ten days after the order, of the fact of the order and the following:
1. Name, trade name, age, and address of the recipient ordered to return subsidies; for a corporation or organization, its name and address and its representative's name, age, and address;
2. Specific grounds for the return order;
3. The subsidy amount the recipient must return;
4. Other matters the head considers necessary for execution of the return order.

Article 21 (Criteria for Imposition and Collection of Sanction Surcharges and Additional Charges)
① Criteria for imposing sanction surcharges under Article 35(1) of the Act shall be as specified in attached Table 2. <Amended May 16, 2023>
② "Where grounds prescribed by Presidential Decree exist, such as imposition of a fine, minor fine, confiscation, additional collection, penalty surcharge, or administrative fine under this or another Act" in the proviso to the portion other than the subparagraphs of Article 35(1) of the Act means cases in which a fine, minor fine, confiscation, additional collection, penalty surcharge, or administrative fine (hereinafter in this Article "administrative fines, etc.") has been imposed under the Act or another Act.
③ When imposing and collecting a sanction surcharge from operators, etc., under Article 35(1) of the Act, the head shall state the type of violation, surcharge amount, and other relevant matters and provide written notification requiring payment.
④ The head shall ensure that the sum of administrative fines, etc., under paragraph 2 and the sanction surcharge does not exceed five times the total subsidies the operators, etc., must return.
⑤ Operators, etc., notified under paragraph 3 shall pay the sanction surcharge to the collection institution designated by the head within 30 days after receiving notification. However, if a natural disaster, wartime conditions, an incident, or another unavoidable cause prevents payment within that period, payment shall be made within seven days after the cause ceases.
⑥ A collection institution receiving payment under paragraph 5 shall issue a receipt to the payer and notify the head without delay of receipt.
⑦ "Cases prescribed by Presidential Decree" in Article 35(3)5 of the Act means cases in which imposition and collection costs exceed the surcharge to be imposed and collected.
⑧ Additional charges under Article 35(4) of the Act shall be calculated as follows:
1. Payment within one month after the surcharge payment deadline: two percent of the overdue amount. However, payment within seven days after the deadline shall incur one percent of the overdue amount;
2. Payment after one month has elapsed from the deadline: the additional charge under the main clause of subparagraph 1 plus an additional charge of one percent of the overdue amount for every month elapsed from the deadline.
⑨ Detailed matters concerning imposition and collection of sanction surcharges and additional charges, other than those in paragraphs 1 through 8, shall be prescribed by Ordinance of the Ministry of the Interior and Safety.

Article 21-2 (Criteria for Payment of Reporting Rewards)
① Where a report or complaint is made under Article 36-3(1) of the Act, the head shall investigate relevant facts, decide whether to pay a reward based on the outcome, and notify the reporter or complainant of the decision.
② Notification under paragraph 1 shall be made after revocation of the grant decision under Article 12(1) of the Act or an order to return subsidies under Article 31(1) or 34(1) of the Act.
③ The head shall pay the reward to the reporter or complainant within 60 days after notification under paragraph 1.
④ The reward under paragraph 3 shall be 30 percent of the amount for which the grant decision was revoked or return was ordered. However, where the reporter's or complainant's contribution makes payment of a reward different from that under the main clause (hereinafter "original reporting reward") necessary, a reward may be paid as follows:
1. Where a reduction is necessary: payment shall be at least 20 percent but less than 30 percent of the amount revoked or ordered returned;
2. Where payment above the original reporting reward is necessary, limited to an original reward of less than five million won: determine the minimum reward amount necessary (hereinafter "minimum payment amount") and pay that minimum only if the original reporting reward is below it. The minimum payment amount shall not exceed five million won.
⑤ No reward shall be paid to a person making a report or complaint with the same contents after a report or complaint under Article 36-3(1) of the Act. Where two or more persons jointly report or complain, the reward shall be paid to their designated representative.
⑥ Matters necessary for reward criteria, methods, and procedures other than those in paragraphs 1 through 5 shall be prescribed by municipal ordinance.

Article 21-3 (Entrustment of Duties) Under Article 36-5 of the Act, the Minister of the Interior and Safety and heads of local governments shall entrust the following to the Korea Local Information Research and Development Institute under Article 72 of the Electronic Government Act:
1. Operation of the integrated local government subsidy management network;
2. Processing of materials or information in the subparagraphs of Article 28-4(1) of the Act;
3. Operation of the online service system under Article 36-4 of the Act.

Article 22 (Processing of Unique Identifying Information) Where unavoidable to perform any of the following duties, the head of a local government may process materials containing resident registration numbers, passport numbers, driver's license numbers, or alien registration numbers under Article 19 of the Enforcement Decree of the Personal Information Protection Act: <Amended October 4, 2023>
1. Duties concerning restrictions on property disposal under Article 21 of the Act;
2. Deleted. <October 4, 2023>
3. Duties concerning publication of lists under Article 30 of the Act;
4. Duties concerning exclusion from project performance under Article 32 of the Act;
5. Duties concerning recovery of subsidies from recipients under Article 34 of the Act;
6. Duties concerning imposition and collection of sanction surcharges and additional charges under Article 35 of the Act;
7. Duties concerning compulsory collection under Article 36 of the Act;
7-2. Duties concerning payment of reporting rewards under Article 36-3 of the Act;
8. Duties concerning establishment, operation, and management of the network and subsidy management using it.

ADDENDA <Presidential Decree No. 31883, July 13, 2021>

Article 1 (Enforcement Date)
This Decree shall enter into force on July 13, 2021.

Article 2 (Special Cases Concerning the Period for Selection of Auditors by Specific Local Government Subsidized Operators)
Notwithstanding Article 11(1), a specific local government subsidized operator that received local government subsidies before this Decree enters into force shall select an auditor within three months from the date this Decree enters into force.

Article 3 (Transitional Measures Concerning Standards, Methods, and Procedures for Payment of Rewards for Reporting)
Until a municipal ordinance under Article 14(6) concerning the standards, methods, procedures, and other matters for payment of rewards for reporting is newly enacted and enters into force, Article 37-7(4) of the former Enforcement Decree of the Local Finance Act (meaning the version before amendment under Article 4(3) of these Addenda) shall apply.

Article 4 (Amendments to Other Statutes and Regulations)
(1) The Enforcement Decree of the Corporate Tax Act is partially amended as follows:
In the former part of Article 64(2), "Local Finance Act" is replaced with "Act on Local Government Subsidy Management".
(2) The Enforcement Decree of the Local Allocation Tax Act is partially amended as follows:
In Article 12(1)1-3, "Article 32-2(2) of the Local Finance Act" is replaced with "the former part of Article 6(2) of the Act on Local Government Subsidy Management", and "the same paragraph" is replaced with "the former part of the same paragraph"; in subparagraph 1-4 of the same paragraph, "Article 32-2(3) of the Local Finance Act" is replaced with "Article 26(2) of the Act on Local Government Subsidy Management"; in subparagraph 1-5 of the same paragraph, "Article 32-2(5) of the Local Finance Act" is replaced with "Article 6(3) of the Act on Local Government Subsidy Management"; in subparagraph 1-6 of the same paragraph, "Article 32-4(1) of the Local Finance Act" is replaced with "Article 13 of the Act on Local Government Subsidy Management"; in subparagraph 1-7 of the same paragraph, "Article 32-4(2) of the Local Finance Act" is replaced with "Article 14 of the Act on Local Government Subsidy Management", and "the same paragraph" is replaced with "the same Article"; and in subparagraph 1-8 of the same paragraph, "Article 32-8(2) and (3) of the Local Finance Act" is replaced with "Article 31(1) and (2) of the Act on Local Government Subsidy Management".
(3) The Enforcement Decree of the Local Finance Act is partially amended as follows:
Articles 37 and 37-2 through 37-7 are deleted.
(4) The Enforcement Decree of the Local Accounting Act is partially amended as follows:
In subparagraph 2 of Article 3, "Article 32-6 of the Local Finance Act" is replaced with "Article 17 of the Act on Local Government Subsidy Management".

Article 5 (Relationship to Other Statutes and Regulations)
Where other statutes and regulations cite the former Enforcement Decree of the Local Finance Act or its provisions concerning the management and operation of local government subsidies when this Decree enters into force, and this Decree contains corresponding provisions, they shall be deemed to cite this Decree or its corresponding provisions in place of the former Enforcement Decree of the Local Finance Act or its provisions.

