Standards for Imposition of Sanction Surcharges (Related to Article 21(1))

■ Enforcement Decree of the Act on Local Government Subsidy Management [Annex 2] <Amended on May 16, 2023>

Standards for Imposition of Sanction Surcharges (Related to Article 21(1))

1. A sanction surcharge shall be calculated by multiplying the amount of local government subsidies to be returned by the applicable surcharge rate in the following table.

| Grounds for imposition and persons subject to imposition | Violation | Surcharge rate |
| --- | --- | --- |
| (a) A local government subsidized operator falling under Article 35(1)1 of the Act | 1) Obtaining the grant of local government subsidies by a false application or other improper means | 500% |
| (a) The same operator | 2) Using local government subsidies for purposes other than their intended purpose | 300% |
| (a) The same operator | 3) Violating statutes and regulations, municipal ordinances, the details of a decision to grant local government subsidies, or a disposition made by the head of a local government under statutes and regulations | 200% |
| (b) A local government subsidy recipient falling under Article 35(1)2 of the Act | 1) Receiving payment of local government subsidies by fraud or other improper means | 500% |
| (b) The same recipient | 2) Using local government subsidies for purposes other than the purpose of payment | 300% |
| (b) The same recipient | 3) Being found not to meet the requirements for receiving local government subsidies | 100% |

2. Where a violation under item (a)2), (a)3), or (b)2) of paragraph 1 results from minor negligence or error, the imposing authority may reduce the sanction surcharge calculated under paragraph 1 by up to one half.
3. Where a violation under paragraph 1(b)3) results from a cause for which the relevant local government subsidy recipient is not responsible, the imposing authority may exempt all or part of the sanction surcharge calculated under paragraph 1.
